# ZOOM-BOUNCE-1: reproduce the owner's reversing wheel sequence without them, at the same
# cursor position (window px 1080, 635 of 2560x1369) and window size. Each leg is one larger
# wheel event (a fast flick), with the owner's own shape (two out, two in, four out, then the
# mirror back) repeated 5 times here. Run with (needs the original game files and a GPU):
#   python -I tools/test/viewer_wiring.py <exe> zoom_bounce_1 <out dir> --gpu --trace
#     --env ANNO_VIEW_SIZE=2560x1369 --app-arg --play --app-arg data/maps/lan5.txt
#     --app-arg --construction-menu --app-arg on --app-arg --water --app-arg enhanced
# then check <out dir>.trace/frames.tsv (view/group/scale per frame) for a one-frame
# disagreement. The REPORTS evidence run used 50 repeats (240 reversal legs); regenerate a
# longer version with the same shape by editing the repeat count in a copy of this file.
look 1080 635
wait ms 1500
# repeat 0
wheel -12 1080 635
wait ms 25
